# Harr host adapter: ZCode keeps the LeanCTX MCP for CodeGraph/service gateway only.
# Native ZCode tools are the primary investigation path; CTX_* entries name the
# primary tool for each shared routing rule, not necessarily a LeanCTX tool id.
CTX_READ='native Read'
CTX_SHELL='mcp__lean-ctx__ctx_shell'
CTX_SEARCH='native Grep'
CTX_GLOB='native Glob'
CTX_TOOLS='mcp__lean-ctx__ctx_tools'
CTX_CALL='mcp__lean-ctx__ctx_call'
HOST_ORCHESTRATION_POLICY='- ZCode orchestration economy: keep sequential implementation in the root chat (GLM Flash); do not spawn subagents merely to move implementation context out of the root. Spawn native subagents only for genuinely independent parallel scopes. The root owns decomposition and integration; give each subagent a bounded, self-sufficient scope and avoid dependencies between active subagents. While a subagent is active, it owns that delegated scope; the root and sibling subagents must not duplicate it. Subagents never spawn/fork agents or invoke Asa themselves; the root is the sole agent router. If a subagent reaches an unresolved material architecture decision, pause that scope and return compact evidence instead of choosing locally. On that escalation, the root must not reread or re-analyze the delegated scope: it may add only already-known global/user constraints, route the compact handoff through $asa, then forward the decision/invariants back to the SAME subagent. For an unresolved material architecture decision discovered directly by the root, the root gathers missing repository/runtime/contract facts under the normal Harr Workspace/tool-routing policy before invoking $asa, but once the boundary is material the root must not invent, rank, compare, or choose architecture alternatives. Asa is the persistent saved workflow asa (the architect runs on the model configured for Asa) routed only through the $asa skill: root passes the root session id, the mode and the exact question, and the workflow architect reads the root chat history itself — root never pre-curates the context. The run executes in the background; wait for its completion notification. If CreateWorkflow or the saved asa workflow is unavailable, report that ZCode Asa orchestration requires it and do not answer the material decision as root. Every Asa request declares mode=architecture-decision, mode=user-dialogue, or mode=explicit-analysis. The root transparently routes requests the user addresses to Asa and faithfully relays the Asa answer instead of answering for Asa; Asa analyzes only supplied material and never broadens into repository discovery. After Asa returns the requested decision or analysis, the existing implementation owner/context continues.'
HOST_NATIVE_POLICY='ZCode native-first routing: workspace file reads, searches, and globs use the native ZCode tools (Read/Grep/Glob and the native editor). Never call mcp__lean-ctx__ctx_read, mcp__lean-ctx__ctx_search, mcp__lean-ctx__ctx_glob, or mcp__lean-ctx__ctx_call. Shell work goes through mcp__lean-ctx__ctx_shell, which caps every response at the 4096-fresh-token turn budget with archive and ctx_expand recovery; mcp__lean-ctx__ctx_tools serves CodeGraph and the enabled service MCPs (and named Ein executors when configured).'
